From: PowOS <noreply@powback.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kicker: Application Dashboard categories respond to a tap

A category was applied on click from currentIndex, which only hover set: a touch tap (no hover) re-applied
the previous category. The click now selects the clicked category first.
---
--- a/applets/kicker/DashboardRepresentation.qml
+++ b/applets/kicker/DashboardRepresentation.qml
@@ -900,7 +900,16 @@
                             baseModel: filterList.model
                             favoritesModel: baseModel.favoritesModel
 
-                            onClicked: ListView.view.applyFilter()
+                            // PowOS: the clicked category, not the hovered one. Hover set currentIndex and the click
+                            // applied it - a tap has no hover, so tapping a category re-applied the previous one
+                            // (mouse and a dragged finger worked, a tap didn't).
+                            onClicked: {
+                                if (isSeparator) {
+                                    return;
+                                }
+                                filterList.currentIndex = index;
+                                filterList.applyFilter();
+                            }
 
                             onHoveredChanged: {
                                 if (hovered && !isSeparator && !ActionMenu.opened) {
